# Code owners for security-critical admission surfaces.
#
# STATUS: NOT ENFORCED FOR MERGE.
#
# Two distinct behaviors must not be conflated:
#   - GitHub may automatically REQUEST review from an owner listed here as
#     soon as this file exists. That is advisory.
#   - GitHub only REQUIRES an owner's approval before merging when branch
#     protection enables required pull-request reviews with "Require review
#     from Code Owners".
#
# As of 2026-08-03 `main` has `required_pull_request_reviews: null`, so no
# approval here is mandatory and no merge is blocked by this file. Enabling
# required reviews on a single-maintainer repository would block all work,
# since GitHub does not permit self-approval.
#
# Do not treat the presence of this file as evidence that these paths were
# reviewed before merging.

# The admission validator decides what may enter the repository. A change here
# changes what every future change is checked against.
/tools/admission_root_v1.py                  @jasonewillis

# Ownership map for the paths above. Listed so that, once required code-owner
# approval is ever enabled, this file cannot be weakened or removed without the
# same approval it grants — otherwise the protections below could be dismantled
# in one pull request and exploited in the next.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @jasonewillis

# PROPOSED PATH, NOT YET IMPLEMENTED. `tools/admission_root_next_v1.py` does
# not exist on `main`, and `tools/admission_root_v1.py` contains no staged-
# successor promotion rule today. Under the issue #65 design (prototyped, not
# adopted) this path would hold pre-authorized replacement bytes that a later
# pull request could promote into the validator position. It is listed before
# it exists so that it is owned from its first commit rather than afterwards.
# If issue #65 is resolved a different way, delete this entry.
/tools/admission_root_next_v1.py             @jasonewillis

# The workflow that supplies base-owned authority values to the validator.
/.github/workflows/candidate-admission.yml   @jasonewillis

